test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:15:36:
   |
15 | missing :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.toggle
   |                                    ^
core.toggle takes an input, a core.TodoId; give it in parentheses: >> core.toggle(...)

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:16:49:
   |
16 | extra core.TodoId#id :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.stop(id)
   |                                                 ^
core.stop takes no input; write >> core.stop alone

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:17:47:
   |
17 | wrong core.Title#t :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.toggle(t)
   |                                               ^
core.toggle takes a core.TodoId, but this gives a core.Title

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:18:64:
   |
18 | primed core.TodoId#id :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.toggle(id')
   |                                                                ^
the input of a dispatch takes no prime (')

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:19:73:
   |
19 | named core.TodoId#id :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.toggle(core.TodoId#x)
   |                                                                         ^
the input of a dispatch names no value; write a name the transition gives, or a value

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:20:48:
   |
20 | unknown :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.toggle(nobody)
   |                                                ^
unknown name nobody; name a value with #nobody in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-dispatch.sumspec:21:65:
   |
21 | pair core.TodoId#id :: Mode.On -> Mode.Off  >> core.rename(id * id)
   |                                                                 ^
factor core.TodoId is written twice

